Before starting work, read the NEWEST file in `docs/agent-sync/` (dated
cross-assistant session briefs from Claude Code / Codex / Cursor sessions).
It records owner directives, in-flight agents and their branches/worktrees,
uncommitted WIP that is not yours, and prod measurements — so parallel
assistants do not collide, re-fix already-fixed defects, or contradict an
owner directive issued in another chat.

Latest as of 2026-08-03: `docs/agent-sync/2026-08-03-claude-session-sync.md`.

When you finish a substantial session, append your own dated brief to
`docs/agent-sync/` in the same shape (directives, shipped, in-flight, traps).
